@page "/components/collapsible"

<PageTitle>Collapsible — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Collapsible</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code>. The whole state machine is the
    element: no compiler, no state, and nothing to restore after a fragment swap.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="CollapsibleBasic.razor"><CollapsibleBasic /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Settings Panel</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Worth knowing before you rely on it either way: the fields inside a closed
    <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> are still in the form and still post.
</p>
<Example Source="CollapsibleSettings.razor"><CollapsibleSettings /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">File Tree</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Nested <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>, and it needs no library: every folder remembers its own
    open state, the keyboard works, and Find in Page reaches inside a closed one in most browsers.
</p>
<Example Source="CollapsibleFileTree.razor"><CollapsibleFileTree /></Example>

